  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Freedom Concert (For Human Rights)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Freedom Concert is the commemoration of 74 years of the adoption of the Universal Declaration of Human Rights (UDHR). Amnesty International has raised human rights awareness and financial support for community-based human rights defenders for fifty years through public musical concerts. This concert serves as a platform to amplify artists&apos; voices in promoting human rights, connect young people to the human rights movement, build solidarity, nurture actors, and advocate for human rights using music and spoken word poetry. The concert celebrates Kenya&apos;s national values, social cohesion and respect for diversity as Kenya emerges from a highly contested general election. Lastly, the concert will help fundraise in support of the Public Defenders Fund. This will be achieved through corporate sponsorship and concert ticket sales.</narrative>
  </description>
